LESSON|0|Maxilani's turn.|While exploring the deep, random encounters like this one with deep sea enemies can occur at any time.
[font_size=18][pulse]Press Space, Enter, or click Continue[/pulse][/font_size]|true
LESSON|0|Maxilani's turn.|While exploring the deep, random encounters like this one with deep sea enemies can occur at any time.
[font_size=18][pulse]Press Space, Enter, or click Continue[/pulse][/font_size]|false
LESSON|0|Maxilani's turn.|A fight is turns, one combatant at a time, fastest Agility going first each round. On your turn: Attack (use a base move, or any spell you've learned), Items (use one on any living party member to heal or boost their stats), or Run (leave the fight - not guaranteed to work). The queue bar across the top shows the coming order. Turn order is shown from first at left to last at right in the turn order bar at the top. Turn order is decided by Agility - whoever has the highest goes first. If a move changes someone's Agility, the turn order always updates right away to reflect it.
[font_size=18][pulse]Press Space, Enter, or click Continue[/pulse][/font_size]|true
LESSON|0|Maxilani's turn.|Choose the [color=yellow]highlighted[/color] attack move against the enemy.|false
LESSON|0|Maxilani's turn.|Hover over the enemy you want to attack to see the stat comparison.|false
LESSON|0|Maxilani's turn.|A hit lands only if the attacker's (left stats panel's ACC number) is strictly greater than the defender's current Evasion (right stats panel's EVA number). In this case, the attacker and defender have equal evasion, so the attacker will miss. Evasion is a pool that a successful dodge spends down by however much Accuracy it just beat, and it only refills at the start of that combatant's own next turn. Get baited into dodging early in a turn round and you may have nothing left to dodge with later in the same turn.
[font_size=18][pulse]Press Space, Enter, or click Continue[/pulse][/font_size]|true
LESSON|0|Maxilani's turn.|Electric Touch will lower Angler's Evasion - that's why its EVA number is shown in [color=e65959]red[/color], with the white (-1) next to it showing exactly how much. A stat shown in [color=e65959]red[/color] means its total went down; a stat shown in [color=66e666]green[/color] means its total went up.
[font_size=18][pulse]Press Space, Enter, or click Continue[/pulse][/font_size]|true
LESSON|0|Maxilani's turn.|Electric Touch will lower Angler's Evasion - that's why its EVA number is shown in [color=e65959]red[/color], with the white (-1) next to it showing exactly how much. A stat shown in [color=e65959]red[/color] means its total went down; a stat shown in [color=66e666]green[/color] means its total went up.
[font_size=18][pulse]Press Space, Enter, or click Continue[/pulse][/font_size]|false
LESSON|0|Maxilani's turn.|Electric Touch's own power is 0. This raw power number is shown in yellow at the top-right of its attack menu button before any stats are added. Add Maxilani's Strength, then subtract Angler's Defense (1-1 = 0), and this attack will deal 1 damage.
[font_size=18][pulse]Press Space, Enter, or click Continue[/pulse][/font_size]|true
LESSON|0|Maxilani's turn.|Click the highlighted Angler to attack.|false
LESSON|0|Electric Touch shocks the target for 1.  EVA -1|Your party's HP is shown in the highlighted purple boxes in the status panels with your party's on the top left and enemies on the top right. HP (health points) red bars end the fight when either all party members or all enemies reach 0. The blue bar underneath each health bar is oxygen which is consumed to cast certain attacks.
[font_size=18][pulse]Press Space, Enter, or click Continue[/pulse][/font_size]|true
LESSON|1|Electric Touch shocks the target for 1.  EVA -1|Your party's HP is shown in the highlighted purple boxes in the status panels with your party's on the top left and enemies on the top right. HP (health points) red bars end the fight when either all party members or all enemies reach 0. The blue bar underneath each health bar is oxygen which is consumed to cast certain attacks.
[font_size=18][pulse]Press Space, Enter, or click Continue[/pulse][/font_size]|false
LESSON|1|Musashi's turn.|Choose the [color=yellow]highlighted[/color] attack move against the enemy.|false
LESSON|1|Musashi's turn.|Hover over the enemy you want to attack to see the stat comparison.|false
LESSON|1|Musashi's turn.|Precise Tap temporarily boosts Musashi's Accuracy stat for this one turn, making the attack much harder to dodge - that's why its ACC number is shown in [color=66e666]green[/color], with the white (+X) next to it showing the increase.
[font_size=18][pulse]Press Space, Enter, or click Continue[/pulse][/font_size]|true
LESSON|1|Musashi's turn.|Click the highlighted Angler to attack.|false
LESSON|2|You land a precise tap for 3.|Click the highlighted Angler to attack.|false
LESSON|2|Bucky's turn.|Choose the [color=yellow]highlighted[/color] attack move against the enemy.|false
LESSON|2|Bucky's turn.|Hover over the enemy you want to attack to see the stat comparison.|false
LESSON|2|Bucky's turn.|Crushing Haymaker hits hard and costs 16 Oxygen, but Bucky's low Accuracy lets enemies dodge it while they have Evasion left. Electric Touch lowers an enemy's Evasion for the rest of the fight. Exhaust that pool first, then a heavy swing can connect.
[font_size=18][pulse]Press Space, Enter, or click Continue[/pulse][/font_size]|true
LESSON|2|Bucky's turn.|Click the highlighted Angler to attack.|false
LESSON|3|You wind up and crush it - Angler evades!|Click the highlighted Angler to attack.|false
LESSON|3|You wind up and crush it - Angler evades!|Sometimes during an enemy's attack, a Quick Time Event shows up:|true
LESSON|3|You wind up and crush it - Angler evades!|Sometimes during an enemy's attack, a Quick Time Event shows up:|false
LESSON|3|Angler uses Bite: Bucky QTE dodge.|Sometimes during an enemy's attack, a Quick Time Event shows up:|false
LESSON|3|Musashi's turn.|Choose the [color=yellow]highlighted[/color] attack move against the enemy.|false
LESSON|3|Musashi's turn.|Hover over the enemy you want to attack to see the stat comparison.|false
LESSON|3|Musashi's turn.|Weaken deals no damage at all - its power is 0, so there's nothing to subtract from Angler's HP. What it does instead is lower their Defense, which is why its DEF number is shown in [color=e65959]red[/color], with the white (-2) next to it. Some moves only ever affect an enemy's stats like this, with no damage of their own, but they're worth using to weaken enemies for greater party hits.
[font_size=18][pulse]Press Space, Enter, or click Continue[/pulse][/font_size]|true
LESSON|3|Musashi's turn.|Click the highlighted Angler to attack.|false
LESSON|4|This enemy's Defense can't be lowered any further!|Click the highlighted Angler to attack.|false
LESSON|4|Maxilani's turn.|Choose the [color=yellow]highlighted[/color] attack move against the enemy.|false
LESSON|4|Maxilani's turn.|Hover over the highlighted button to see what Flash Blast does.|false
LESSON|4|Maxilani's turn.|Flash Blast deals no damage either, same as Weaken - instead it hits every enemy at once with a status called Blindness, which lowers Agility, Accuracy, and Defense all by the same amount at once. That's why the enemy's ACC and DEF numbers are both shown in [color=e65959]red[/color] here: lower Accuracy means their own attacks miss more, and lower Defense means your hits deal more damage to them. Flash Blast subtracts 2 from all three, for as many turns as Maxilani's own Accuracy. Blindness is only one of several status conditions moves can inflict - hover over any attack that names one on its own button (like Scuba Stabbing's Bleed) to see exactly what it does, or find full details on all of them, including ones not shown in this fight, from the Combat Help tab of the Esc menu out in the world.
[font_size=18][pulse]Press Space, Enter, or click Continue[/pulse][/font_size]|true
LESSON|4|Maxilani's turn.|Click the highlighted All enemies to attack.|false
LESSON|5|Flash Blast: Angler affected.|Click the highlighted All enemies to attack.|false
LESSON|5|Flash Blast: Angler affected.|Now defeat the enemy for real to finish the lesson! Winning a battle awards XP to your whole party, not just whoever fought including anyone who went down during the fight, who gains XP the same as everyone else. Gain enough XP and a diver levels up, which refills their HP and Oxygen even if they went down. Otherwise a downed diver needs a Revive spell to get back on their feet. Leveling up doesn't change your combat stats but instead lets the divers gain new abilities.
[font_size=18][pulse]Press Space, Enter, or click Continue[/pulse][/font_size]|true
LESSON|5|Flash Blast: Angler affected.|Winning won't grant any XP or rewards in this case but makes for good practice. There's no real risk in fighting this one out - a loss just sends the party back to the overworld to regroup, fully healed.
[font_size=18][pulse]Press Space, Enter, or click Continue[/pulse][/font_size]|true
